{"ts": 0.103928, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m──\u001b[0m \u001b[90mStage 4 · Commands and streams\u001b[0m \u001b[90m────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m \u001b[90m○\u001b[0m\u001b[90m○\u001b[0m\u001b[90m○\u001b[0m\u001b[93m◉\u001b[0m\u001b[90m○\u001b[0m  \u001b[93m4.2\u001b[0m \u001b[90m──\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 255}
{"ts": 0.103968, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\r\n", "len": 2}
{"ts": 0.10403, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97mSpaces and quotes\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nThe shell splits a line on spaces. Quote a name that has a space.\r\n", "len": 99}
{"ts": 0.104068, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\r\n  \u001b[92mtouch my notes.txt\u001b[0m       \u001b[90m# two files: my, and notes.txt\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mls\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mtouch \"my notes.txt\"\u001b[0m     \u001b[90m# one file with a space in its name\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mls\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nIt is the same for every command: \u001b[92mvim my notes.txt\u001b[0m would open two\r\nfiles; \u001b[92mvim \"my notes.txt\"\u001b[0m opens one.\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m▶ Try them, then type \u001b[92mnext\u001b[93m.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 370}
{"ts": 0.10754, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;90mnext\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mshow\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mprev\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mquit\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 71}
{"ts": 0.107832, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 251}
