{"ts": 0.256354, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97mMany names at once\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[92m*\u001b[0m matches any run of characters in a file name. The shell fills in\r\n", "len": 110}
{"ts": 0.256384, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "the names before the command runs.\r\n\r\n  \u001b[92mls *.txt\u001b[0m         \u001b[90m# every name ending in .txt\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mwc -l *.txt\u001b[0m      \u001b[90m# count the lines in each one\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nA name with \u001b[92m*\u001b[0m in it is called a \u001b[1mglob\u001b[0m. Predict before you act: \u001b[92mrm *\u001b[0m\r\nwould remove everything in the folder.\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m▶ Try both, then type \u001b[92mnext\u001b[93m for Stage 4's task.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 381}
