{"ts": 0.360368, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97mSTAGE 4 — GATE TASK\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nDo these:\r\n  1. Use \u001b[92mseq\u001b[0m and a pipe: count the lines of \u001b[92mseq 1 100\u001b[0m and\r\n", "len": 124}
{"ts": 0.360411, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "     save that number to count.txt.\r\n  2. Use a glob to list every *.txt file in this folder.\r\n\r\nThen type \u001b[92mcheck\u001b[0m.\r\n\u001b[90mI will check: count.txt exists and contains 100, and that you\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90mlisted the .txt files with a glob.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90mThis task runs in /var/folders/jx/f_4n055973x5cwnyh_mhlw9h0000gn/T/shelltutor-sim-home-qiegw_c0/stage4; \u001b[92mpwd\u001b[90m shows it.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m▶ Type \u001b[92mcheck\u001b[93m when done.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 429}
